.TH "RAPTOR-CONVERT" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-convert \- convert between .rbd, .rbds and AWB .awb
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor convert\fR [\-h] [\-\-to {rbd,rbds,awb}] [\-\-allow\-lossy] [\-\-strict] [\-f {text,json,markdown}] [\-\-report FILE] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-no\-sidecar] [\-\-normalize\-out FILE] IN OUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write IN as OUT in the format OUT's extension names (or \-\-to). AWB conversions print a summary of the features the destination cannot represent. Refuses a lossy .rbd conversion unless \-\-allow\-lossy.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI{rbd|rbds|awb}\fR
format to write (default: OUT's extension)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-lossy\fR
\&.rbds\-only content (annotations, experiment settings, rate definitions) is dropped in .rbd; AWB conversions report their losses instead and do not need this switch
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
AWB only: write nothing and exit 4 if the summary reports any feature the destination cannot use
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|markdown}\fR
AWB summary format (default text)
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR \fIFILE\fR
AWB only: also write the summary as Markdown to FILE
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
AWB only: print the summary and write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-sidecar\fR
AWB only: do not write the .raptor.json sidecar of RAPTOR\-only metadata
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR
AWB only: write a reduced RAPTOR model carrying only what the AWB file represents, and export that
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
